<title>UK: Chase Capital II sets $500 million 30-year FRN. [Corrected 14:30 gmt]</title>
<headline>Chase Capital II sets $500 million 30-year FRN. [Corrected 14:30 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Lead manager corrects name of borrower from &quot;Chase Capital III&quot;)</p>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Chase, Goldman Sachs International and Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CHASE CAPITAL II</p>
<p> AMT    $500 MLN	SPREAD     +50 BP    MATURITY    01.FEB.27</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 BASE	 3M LIBOR  PAY DATE   L24.JAN.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A1	  ISS PRICE  ***	 FULL FEES   1.0 PCT</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   BBB+	REOFFER    ***</p>
<p> NOTES	*** TO BE PRICED 59 TO 61 B.P. OVER LIBOR</p>
<p>		L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> LISTING    UNLISTED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
